&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally posted at:
&lt;a class="link" href="https://huggingface.co/blog/RDTvlokip/when-your-neural-network-needs-anger-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;https://huggingface.co/blog/RDTvlokip/when-your-neural-network-needs-anger-management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-conclusion"&gt;🎯 Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Batch Normalization &lt;strong&gt;revolutionized deep learning&lt;/strong&gt; in 2015 by making very deep networks
trainable. From &lt;strong&gt;ResNet&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;Inception&lt;/strong&gt; to modern architectures, BatchNorm is &lt;strong&gt;everywhere&lt;/strong&gt;
in CNNs. Despite alternatives (&lt;strong&gt;LayerNorm&lt;/strong&gt; for Transformers, &lt;strong&gt;GroupNorm&lt;/strong&gt; for small
batches), BatchNorm remains the &lt;strong&gt;standard for computer vision&lt;/strong&gt;. The exact mechanism is still
&lt;strong&gt;debated&lt;/strong&gt; (internal covariate shift? loss landscape smoothing?), but the &lt;strong&gt;results speak&lt;/strong&gt;:
faster, more stable, more accurate training. BatchNorm = &lt;strong&gt;essential tool&lt;/strong&gt; in the deep learning toolbox! 🚀⚡&lt;/p&gt;
